From 89055a704bb85bb8aced04b80518682193a06a28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:21:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] A Rogue's afterimage can be lit toward its colour, a pale
 ghost of light

Basin Battle, the thirty-fourth round (HasActionCombat() 34). The colour PlayUnitAfterimage takes
may be "AARRGGBB": its top byte is a light (0 to 255), and the copy is lit that far toward the
colour, after its own lighting and before the fog, so the body's shape and shading still show
under it. A six-digit colour is a plain tint, as before. A tint only multiplies the light, so a
copy of a dark-clad Rogue under a cool tint read as a dark smear, never a pale copy. The light
rides the instance tint word's top byte (instance_tint::pack_lit), which pack keeps at 0xff.
